# Assessments & Admin Suite Implementation - Completed

We are adding two critical components to the SkillPilot platform:
1. **Course Assessments**: A testing system integrated into courses. Passing a final assessment is required for certificate eligibility.
2. **Admin Suite**: A centralized management interface for platform administrators to oversee all tenants, users, and courses.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The Admin Suite will provide global, cross-tenant access. This requires a dedicated [Admin](file:///d:/learning/SkillPilot/skillpilot-frontend/src/app/%28dashboard%29/admin/users/page.tsx#28-126) module and specialized backend controllers that override tenant scoping.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Assessments Module (Backend)

#### [NEW] Data Model
- **Quiz**: `title`, `description`, `passing_score`, `time_limit`. Linked to [Course](file:///d:/learning/SkillPilot/skillpilot-frontend/src/app/%28dashboard%29/courses/page.tsx#13-23).
- **Question**: `text`, `type` (MCQ/TF), `quiz_id`.
- **Option**: `text`, `is_correct`, `question_id`.
- **QuizAttempt**: `user_id`, `quiz_id`, `score`, `status`.

---

### 2. Admin Suite (Backend & Frontend)

#### [NEW] [Admin Module (Backend)](file:///d:/learning/SkillPilot/skillpilot-backend/Modules/Admin)
- Specialized controllers for:
  - `GlobalTenantController`: Manage all active/inactive workspaces.
  - `GlobalUserController`: Manage all users across the platform.
  - `GlobalCourseController`: Review and manage all hosted courses.

#### [MODIFY] [Sidebar.tsx](file:///d:/learning/SkillPilot/skillpilot-frontend/src/components/shared/Sidebar.tsx)
- Expand Admin links to include:
  - **Tenants** (Global view)
  - **Users** (Global list)
  - **Courses** (Global review)
  - **Assessments** (Global analytics)

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests - COMPLETED
- `php artisan test Modules/Assessments`: PASS (Verified Quiz/Question/Option logic).
- `php artisan test Modules/Admin`: PASS (Verified Global Tenant/User/Course access).
- `npx eslint`: PASS (Verified all frontend components are free of `any` types).

### Manual Verification
1. Login as Admin and verify access to all global dashboards.
2. As a student, complete all lessons and pass the final quiz.
3. Verify that the certificate is generated only after a passing quiz attempt.
